SWEET WLAN stage 3 run E (patch 0133, docs/research/43a-xnu-stage3-chip-writes.md rows W15-W17, docs/research/43c-run-e-release.md), boot-arg sweetwlan=7 (= run D of 0132, then W16 + W17; levels 1-6 behave as in 0132). THE FIRST TIME A CPU RUNS ON THE CHIP.
W15 (cfg 0x88 |= 0x300, DHD dhd_pcie.c:2223-2228) is NOT implemented: a config write DHD makes at attach, effect on this run unknown (43c X5), a halted-core bus hang cannot be bounded; the poll may then see a stale word (informative timeout).
W16: checks (image, pin, vector at bp 0 still there, PCIe core mailbox mask 0xC34 must be 0 and the host controller's ELBI IRQ0/1/2 enables 0x10/0x14/0x18 must all be 0 = IRQ gate, read only; poll window cfg 0x84, token baseline), then the CA7 release = DHD si_core_reset(0,0): RESET_CTL 1, IOCTL 0x3, RESET_CTL 0, IOCTL 0x1 (aiutils.c:1242-1325). W17: poll ram_end-4, 100 x 50 ms, every change printed; shared address checked, version byte read; ALWAYS the stop action (CA7 RESET_CTL := 1 read back, cfg 0x84 := 0) on success and on every failure.
Pure part (bsd/dev/sweet_wlan_wr.h): 6 new deny-by-default tuples (run 5, once; release tuples need SWF_RELOK), done mask 64 bit, two new read ranges (mailbox, ELBI irq block), swl_idle_wait in swl_restore, swl_w16_rev_ok. Review 0133 F1-F4: restore re-halts the CA7 when only the EP Command check failed and memory decode is on and BAR0 is unchanged; config restore rows are skipped when the link checks 1..4 fail; SWF_W16 is set just before the starting store; the CA7 summary and halted use the CA7 row's own read-back (ca_ok). Glue (bsd/dev/sweet_wlan.c): sw3_ca7_ok/sw3_ca7_bit limit the CA7 wrapper stores (CPUHALT-clear IOCTL and the starting RESET_CTL := 0 only at level 7, each once, in order); level 7 runs as 6 unless PCIe core rev 64..73.
Final line: "SWEET WLAN: stage 3 level 7 done shared=<hex> version=<n> polls=<n> halted=1". HW-WRITE path: Opus review round 1 applied (docs/reviews/0133-wlan-arm-release.md), not yet re-reviewed.

